This project is a Kotlin port of
"amazon-sns-java-extended-client-lib"
(https://github.com/awslabs/amazon-sns-java-extended-client-lib):

    Copyright 2010-2020 Amazon.com, Inc. or its affiliates. All Rights Reserved.
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

This is a derivative work under the Apache License, Version 2.0. The message-offload
control flow, message-attribute validation, and S3 key prefix rules in
src/main/kotlin/com/christophsens/snsoverflow/SnsExtendedClient.kt, SnsExtendedClientConfig.kt,
and SnsExtendedClientConstants.kt are ported from the corresponding logic in the original's
AmazonSNSExtendedClient, AmazonSNSExtendedClientBase, AmazonSNSExtendedClientUtil,
SNSExtendedClientConstants, and SNSExtendedClientConfiguration, translated from Java to Kotlin.
The RESERVED_ATTRIBUTE_NAME value and S3 key prefix validation rules are themselves ported from
amazon-sqs-java-extended-client-lib's SQSExtendedClientConstants
(https://github.com/awslabs/amazon-sqs-java-extended-client-lib), which the original SNS library
depends on directly for these constants. See the copyright header in each file for the original
attribution.

Changes made in this port:

  * The original's separate AmazonSNSExtendedClient (SnsClient) and
    AmazonSNSExtendedAsyncClient (SnsAsyncClient) are consolidated into a single
    SnsExtendedClient, since aws-sdk-kotlin's SnsClient is already suspend-based.
  * The pass-through base class (AmazonSNSExtendedClientBase) is replaced by Kotlin interface
    delegation (`SnsClient by snsClient`).
  * payloadoffloading-common (PayloadStore/S3BackedPayloadStore/S3Dao/Util) is replaced by
    s3overflow (https://github.com/christoph-sens/s3overflow), itself a from-scratch Kotlin
    reimplementation of payload-offloading-java-common-lib-for-aws.
  * SNSExtendedClientConfiguration's ObjectCannedACL/ServerSideEncryptionStrategy
    configuration and the deprecated pre-PayloadStorageConfiguration aliases are dropped.
    Core behavior — threshold-based offloading, alwaysThroughS3, the JSON message-structure
    rejection, message-attribute validation — is preserved.
  * The original's per-message "S3Key" message-attribute override (letting a caller pin the
    exact S3 key for one publish) is dropped in favor of the config-level s3KeyPrefix already
    used by sqsoverflow's SqsExtendedClient, for a consistent configuration surface across
    both ports.
  * publishBatch offloading is new: the original predates SNS's PublishBatch API and only
    overrides publish. This port adds the analogous per-entry offload for publishBatch,
    mirroring the batch handling already present in sqsoverflow's SqsExtendedClient.

The RESERVED_ATTRIBUTE_NAME value ("ExtendedPayloadSize") is kept unchanged from the original
for interop with SQSExtendedClient implementations subscribed to an SNS topic via a raw-delivery
SQS subscription. The pointer JSON format produced by this port is not byte-identical to the
original's (see s3overflow's note on its pointer format); for a fresh build with no existing
Java consumers, that's the simpler choice.

